<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67313" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μηδ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <u>Median</u>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Μηδικά</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πράγματα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the
				Median affairs</i>, esp. <i>the war with the Medes</i>, the
			name given by Gr. historians to the great Persian war, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1303b33
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Μ. πόλεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.90
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				95
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μ. ἐσθής</span>, i.e.
				<i>silken</i> garments, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				1.20
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ-ώτερα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					1.25
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ώτερον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, κατεσκευασμένος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μηδικὴ πόα</span>, <i>lucerne, Medicago
				sativa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				606
			</span></i>; M. alone, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				8.7.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.147
			</span></i> (by some written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδίκη</span>, Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.316
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1967.27
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.43
			</span></i> codd.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδική, ἡ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλένιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				14.108
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλον Μηδικόν</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῆλον</span>
			 (B). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπὸς Μηδικός</span> a form of silphium
			juice, prob. <i>assafoetida</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
				<u>Ven.</u>
				3.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μηδικόν, τό</span>, perh. a tomb <i>in Persian style</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				22.124
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
